        ABOUT US
      </p>
      <h2 style="margin-top:18px">A Small Team<br>That Stays.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="story" data-rv>
        <p>Rimba started in Pontianak in 2019, during a fire season that turned the sky orange for six weeks. The three founders were volunteers then, mapping burn scars on motorbikes and arguing about the same thing on every project they joined: <strong>everyone counted planting days, and nobody counted surviving trees.</strong></p>
        <p>We registered as a foundation the following year and wrote down three rules that still run the place. Crews come from the village and are paid at posted rates. No seedling is ordered before a written agreement is signed. Survival counts are published whether they flatter us or not. Seven years on, we are 23 people, most of them in the field, and the rules have outlasted every grant cycle so far.</p>
        <figure class="quote-card">
          <blockquote>&ldquo;A planting day is a photograph. The work is the five years after it, and that is what we ask people to fund.&rdquo;</blockquote>
          <figcaption>Sari Wulandari, Field Coordinator, Kubu Raya</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="tl" data-rv style="--d:.1s">
        <div class="tl-fill" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="tl-year">2019</p>
          <h3>First canal blocked</h3>
          <p>Eleven volunteers, one peat dome in Kubu Raya, and a dam built from nibung posts and sandbags before the dry season turned.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="tl-year">2020</p>
          <h3>Foundation registered</h3>
          <p>Rimba becomes a legal foundation, and the first village agreement is signed with 34 households along the canal line.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="tl-year">2022</p>
          <h3>Work reaches the coast</h3>
          <p>Mangrove planting starts in Demak with two fishpond cooperatives and the first 4 km of shoreline.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="tl-year">2024</p>
          <h3>Counts go public</h3>
          <p>Survival reporting moves into Field Notes, printed every month with the losses left in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item">
          <span class="tl-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="tl-year">2026</p>
          <h3>64 villages, one book</h3>
          <p>The 64th village agreement is signed. Together they cover 9,412 hectares, every hectare walked and logged by its own patrol.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
